From eeef9e86100420a1de5d3119a4bbca6569f2b598 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Brown <themagnificentmrb@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:27:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix UAE4ARM ARM platform builds

Add explicit Android ARMv7, Android AArch64, and macOS arm64
targets that honor caller-selected compilers and Apple cross-build
settings.

Keep staged FLAC and mpg123 support configurable, and avoid treating
the dynamically loaded capsimg side library as a cross-build
prerequisite.

Make the ARM helpers PIC-safe on ELF and Mach-O, and update legacy
platform code for current Clang, Android, and Apple APIs while
preserving the existing ARMv7 and AArch64 JIT paths. Keep large-file
zfile seeks working on 32-bit Android API 21 through its public
lseek64 interface.
